# dev.kitty-session — HAND-AUTHORED (declarative), tracked in git via stow.
#
# Why not the auto-serialized snapshot: `save_as_session` writes window ids,
# group ids and layout biases (unreadable) and always records plain `claude`,
# so restore starts a BLANK chat. This file instead launches `claude -c`, which
# resumes the most recent conversation for each pane's cwd (Claude stores chats
# per-directory under ~/.claude/projects/<cwd-slug>/). Closest thing to tmux
# persistence without a tmux/zellij layer.
#
# DO NOT overwrite this file with cmd+shift+s. For throwaway snapshots, save
# under a different name; keep this one hand-edited.
#
# Panes:
#   claude -c            -> resume last chat for that dir
#   --var=IS_NVIM=1      -> lets kitty.conf hand ctrl/alt-hjkl to nvim
#   (no cmd)             -> plain shell
# Note: `launch claude -c` closes the pane when claude exits. Want it to drop to
# a shell instead? swap for:  launch zsh -i -c "claude -c; exec zsh -i"

